+// beyond maxStorageBufferRange, and assumes that the scale_x * scale_y host pixels of a guest pixel are consecutive. The resolve shaders store each 16 bytes of guest data
+// (a group of 16 / bpp guest pixels) as scale_x * scale_y consecutive 16-byte blocks, block (rx, ry) = rx * scale_y + ry holding host pixels rx * n .. rx * n + n - 1 of host
+// row ry (see the fused resolve shaders of render_target_cache.cpp, verified bit-identical to the SDK's copies). With this on (the default), the read-back binds only the
+// range it reads and picks, for each guest pixel, the host pixel at the top left (or the center with readback_resolve_half_pixel_offset) of its footprint.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(rcomp_readback_downscale, true, "GPU/Vulkan",
+                    "Read back resolution-scaled resolves with R-comp's downscale (bounded binding, the resolve shaders' scaled layout)")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kRequiresRestart);
